{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787603595207500001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"panicky-sylphish-foxterrier","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"77f58824110b483c69939e480bd93e1f8b02058fac574bb785720c7583583cf0","event_uuid":"94629716-e8c0-40ff-80e0-c95846f0049d","position":{"commit_sha":"ad810bca3c7cbfebfe735ef06997d2d05107b4ce","position":"1787594463836524001-94629716-e8c0-40ff-80e0-c95846f0049d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"17757db8ae32323fa41e791b3cec61aa76a8f4831078511e71ceb33da21eef76","event_uuid":"ecd0d3fb-44de-4c3d-ace1-da468c196ce1","position":{"commit_sha":"a27d90c820cfe512efcf3ace7bf229f1dc151da0","position":"1787594602443752001-ecd0d3fb-44de-4c3d-ace1-da468c196ce1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e7074e504921679ac42132ee1904cf6ccf33515aa9bf5453cb8de6718be65588","event_uuid":"85e9d218-4bcb-4d44-9ee3-0c416abd5966","position":{"commit_sha":"5ade8aaa59d60324b5c59d15e551f2edc110e7fc","position":"1787598310104151001-85e9d218-4bcb-4d44-9ee3-0c416abd5966"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"53e78a132d51ff408124b2333dc1f5b4a86271ee8b3ec1fc1c01eb1c3ceeb9d6","event_uuid":"bceda1ab-a8ff-41d5-9573-e92497d95d05","position":{"commit_sha":"f2cf2513b45048450ee2894cb35b813ba52a2d99","position":"1787598534647758001-bceda1ab-a8ff-41d5-9573-e92497d95d05"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"470cfe13da84738ff735771394225fb8008fdedf23ad5ec3a0a5eb887092fe40","event_uuid":"8eb5c968-24ac-4d4c-9dd2-459bcdf3db9b","position":{"commit_sha":"e82c727fe148f889742ee77af1cbfff6651fe3eb","position":"1787600343830032001-8eb5c968-24ac-4d4c-9dd2-459bcdf3db9b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787594463836524001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ecd0d3fb-44de-4c3d-ace1-da468c196ce1","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"},{"link_uuid":"bceda1ab-a8ff-41d5-9573-e92497d95d05","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fd4a-4e91-f179-4932"}],"description":"Add an `mcp` autodeploy target to `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` (+ the timer) implementing the ADR\n0079 amendment's blue-green pointer-swap, so the on-box `rebar-mcp` service tracks `origin/main`\nwithout ever killing an in-flight certified op. Single concern: the MCP deploy path in autodeploy;\nthe service/edge itself is esok, secrets are avians.\n\n## Approach + rationale (blue-green, per ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur)\nModel the MCP deploy on the LOCAL main-tracking updater (immutable release + atomic pointer swap +\nretire-when-idle), NOT the review-bot stop-and-health-drain. On a detected MCP source change:\n1. Build the new MCP image (tagged by target sha).\n2. Start a NEW `rebar-mcp` container alongside the old (one-in/one-out overlap cap; a memory-pressure\n   pre-check aborts the overlap if the t4g.large 8 GiB box is too tight, alerting instead of risking\n   OOM).\n3. Health-check the new container (`/health` OK) — on failure, discard it and keep the old serving\n   (rollback = do nothing; `current` upstream untouched).\n4. **Atomically flip the nginx `/mcp/` upstream** to the new container (re-point the materialized\n   include + `nginx -s reload`; nginx drains old worker connections gracefully) — the deploy is now\n   done; it never waited on or killed an in-flight op.\n5. **Retire the old container off the critical path**, gated by a flock-style \"still serving?\" check\n   (`/health` in_flight / active connections). Retain the newest N; over a hard cap, emit an SNS\n   alert (the terraform `rebar-gerrit-alerts` topic) rather than killing a live container or growing\n   unbounded — mirroring the local updater's RELEASES_KEEP/RELEASES_CAP + reject-streak alert.\n\nWhy: eliminates review-bot bug 7b4a (a never-idle shared MCP server can't satisfy a gauge-gated\ndrain bound, so the bound is exhausted and an op is killed; a bigger bound only defers it).\nDecoupling retirement from deploy means the deploy never blocks and never kills; a killed op is\nclient-visible + idempotent (event-sourced), so retirement is safe.\n\n## Change detection + blast radius\n`MCP_PATHS` (src/rebar/, Dockerfile.mcp, the mcp compose service, pyproject.toml, plus any mcp entry\nscript) diffed deployed..target triggers ONLY an `mcp` rebuild. Because `src/rebar/` is shared with\nreview-bot, a src change triggers BOTH targets — each is change-detected, drained, and deployed\nINDEPENDENTLY; gerrit is never touched (retain the existing explicit assert on the gerrit container\nid). Rollback to the previous MCP image on health-check failure. `flock` still serializes.\n\n## Portability (blocking `project.portability`)\nThe MCP deploy trigger is the existing on-box `systemd`/`launchd`-style timer polling the git mirror\n— an operation-linked poll, NOT a specific CI provider. No GitHub-Actions-only path; the drain,\nflip, and retire logic run in-process in the script and work with any/no CI.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tier: **real subprocess/bash integration with temp git repos + a fake docker** (test-design §3:\n  \"CLI/env/exit codes\" + \"git refs\"). Oracles, each asserted on real script invocations:\n  - An MCP-only source change (touch a `MCP_PATHS` file between two commits) triggers an `mcp` build\n    and NO review-bot/gerrit rebuild; a review-bot-only change does the inverse; a shared\n    `src/rebar/` change triggers BOTH independently (contrast cases, §6).\n  - The cutover sequence is start-new → health-check → flip-upstream → retire-old (assert ordering\n    via a recorded call log from a stubbed docker/nginx), and the deploy returns success WITHOUT\n    waiting on `in_flight` (assert: with in_flight>0 on the OLD container, the deploy still completes\n    and flips).\n  - Retire honors liveness: an old container reporting in_flight>0 is NOT killed; over the cap an SNS\n    alert is emitted (assert via `REBAR_DEV_ALERT_CMD`-style sink, no real SNS) and no live container\n    is deleted.\n  - Health-check failure on the new container leaves the OLD upstream current (rollback oracle:\n    upstream include unchanged, old container still serving) and a retry succeeds (§5D).\n  - gerrit container id is asserted unchanged across a deploy (blast-radius oracle).\n\n## Compat / rollback / migration-safety\nAdditive to autodeploy (new target); existing review-bot/gerrit behavior unchanged (regression\noracle above). ADR 0079 amendment documents the new target. Rollback = revert the `mcp` branch of\nthe script; review-bot deploy path is independent.\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR), cibophobic-holohedral-esok (switchable upstream +\n`/health`).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"],["depends_on","fd4a-4e91-f179-4932"],["parent","jira-reb-3527"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"jira-reb-3527","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6964-40bb-46c9-48a7","ticket_type":"story","title":"Extend autodeploy (ADR 0079) to an mcp target with its own in-flight drain gate","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["94629716-e8c0-40ff-80e0-c95846f0049d","ecd0d3fb-44de-4c3d-ace1-da468c196ce1","85e9d218-4bcb-4d44-9ee3-0c416abd5966","bceda1ab-a8ff-41d5-9573-e92497d95d05","8eb5c968-24ac-4d4c-9dd2-459bcdf3db9b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787603595207500001,"uuid":"8a80242f-d8f5-48fe-98a2-444531ce7142"}